<div class="waitlist-banner">
  <div class="banner-inner">
    <strong>We’re building local AI with no API token caps.</strong>
    Free Nano + Lite. <strong>Standard $149 once adds Quick / Core / Code / Vision. Pro $30/mo or $249/yr adds Plus 397B.</strong>
    <a href="#support">Become a Founder →</a>
  </div>
</div>

<section class="hero" id="top">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="hero-badge">
      <span class="hero-badge-dot"></span>
      v1.11.79 · notarized Mac DMG · community-funded
    </div>
    <h1>Unlimited <span class="gradient">local usage.</span><br/>Cloud-tool energy. <span class="green-g">On your Mac.</span></h1>
    <p class="hero-sub">
      Outlier is a Mac-native beta app for people who are tired of paying $200/month
      and still hitting usage limits. The goal is simple: <strong>cloud-style coding workflows,
      running locally by default, with no API token caps from Outlier.</strong> The app is early. The mission is not.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="btn btn-green" href="https://github.com/Outlier-host/outlier-app-releases/releases/download/v1.11.79/Outlier-1.11.79-arm64.dmg" target="_blank">Download beta app</a>
      <a class="btn btn-accent" href="#support">Become a Founder</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="#roadmap">See what we’re building</a>
    </div>
    <div class="req">Apple Silicon · macOS 12+ · Free Nano + Lite · Standard $149 adds the mid tiers · Pro $30/mo adds Plus · local by default · performance varies by hardware</div>
    <div class="req" style="max-width:720px;margin:0.6rem auto 0;line-height:1.6;">
      Outlier is actively under development. “Unlimited” means no API token meter from Outlier for local models; speed, context, model fit, and battery life depend on your Mac.
    </div>

    <div class="proof">
      <div class="proof-item">
        <div class="proof-num green">∞</div>
        <div class="proof-label">Local usage</div>
      </div>
      <div class="proof-item">
        <div class="proof-num">$149</div>
        <div class="proof-label">Standard, one time</div>
      </div>
      <div class="proof-item">
        <div class="proof-num purple">$30</div>
        <div class="proof-label">Pro / month</div>
      </div>
      <div class="proof-item">
        <div class="proof-num">$200</div>
        <div class="proof-label">Founders lifetime</div>
      </div>
      <div class="proof-item">
        <div class="proof-num green">100%</div>
        <div class="proof-label">Local by default</div>
      </div>
      <div class="proof-item">
        <div class="proof-num purple">7</div>
        <div class="proof-label">Model tiers</div>
      </div>
      <div class="proof-item">
        <div class="proof-num">0</div>
        <div class="proof-label">Cloud token bill</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="split-hero">
      <div class="hero-panel">
        <h3>The pitch in one sentence</h3>
        <p>
          Cloud coding tools are incredible, but usage caps kill momentum. Outlier is the
          bet that the same style of coding platform can live on your Mac: agent plans,
          file edits, tests, memory, vision, research, and long runs without a meter.
        </p>
        <div class="mini-list">
          <div><b>✓</b><span><b>Free:</b> Nano + Lite for everyday local AI.</span></div>
          <div><b>✓</b><span><b>Standard:</b> $149 once. Adds Quick, Core, Code, Vision. Yours to keep.</span></div>
          <div><b>✓</b><span><b>Pro:</b> $30/month or $249/year. Adds Plus 397B.</span></div>
          <div><b>✓</b><span><b>Founders:</b> $200 once, lifetime Pro, 500 seat cap.</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-panel">
        <h3>What the money funds</h3>
        <p>
          Every dollar goes toward the gap between where Outlier is today and where it needs
          to be: stronger coding models, better agent loops, faster local inference, cleaner
          UX, and public build logs showing exactly how we compress, speed up, test, and ship.
        </p>
        <div class="raise-meter"><span></span></div>
        <p style="font-family:var(--mono); font-size:0.82rem; color:var(--text-dim);">
          Community-funded. Build-in-public. No cloud token tax.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="hardware-matrix" style="padding: 1.5rem 0; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.02); border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.05); border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.05);">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h3 style="font-size: 1rem; text-align: center; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; color: var(--text-muted, #9ca3af); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em;">Will it run on your Mac?</h3>
    <div class="hw-grid" style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: 0.75rem; max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto;">
      <div class="hw-card" style="text-align: center; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 10px; background: rgba(34,197,94,0.06); border: 1px solid rgba(34,197,94,0.18);">
        <div style="font-size: 0.75rem; color: #22c55e; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.06em;">16 GB</div>
        <div style="font-size: 1.05rem; margin: 0.25rem 0; font-weight: 500;">MacBook Air</div>
